# Layer-2 download cache. Fetched per manifest/corpora.yaml, never committed.
# Committing it would drag third-party licenses (Apache-2.0 / CC-BY-4.0 / no license)
# into this MIT repository, which is the very thing splitting the corpus out of the
# tool repository was meant to avoid.
/cache/

# Benchmark artifacts
/results.json
/out/

.DS_Store

# ...except inside corpus/, where three of them are upstream content rather than Finder
# droppings: they are byte-identical to files the pinned skillet-wild commit ships, and
# dropping them made the corpus differ from its upstream for three samples. Worse, they made
# the duplicate report environment-dependent — five groups in a working tree, seven in a
# fresh clone — which is the "validates differently on different machines" defect this
# repository has now fixed twice elsewhere.
!corpus/**/.DS_Store

# Agent worktrees. Temporary checkouts created for isolated subagent runs;
# each is its own git repository and none of it belongs in this one.
/.claude/worktrees/
